[[Meat]] plays a much more dominant role in [[Pakistani cuisine]] as compared to other [[South Asian cuisine]]s. The most popular are [[Chicken (food)|chicken]], [[Lamb and mutton|lamb]], [[beef]], [[Goat meat|goat]], and [[Fish as food|fish]]. Beef is particularly sought after for kebab dishes or the classic beef shank dish [[nihari]]. [[Seafood]] is generally not consumed in large amounts, though it is<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bawarchi.com/cookbook/pakistan.html |title=Bawarchi: Saroj's Cookbook: Pakistani Cuisine |accessdate=2008-09-13 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20080920143457/http://www.bawarchi.com/cookbook/pakistan.html |archivedate=2008-09-20 }}</ref> very popular in the coastal areas of [[Sindh]] and the [[Makran]] coast of [[Balochistan (Pakistan)|Balochistan]].
